ATLAS> # [T] OPTION gate tunnelling mesh: rectangle enclosing only the gate insulator (Al2O3 + HfO2), one y-slice every 0.2 um,
ATLAS> # 0.5 nm points along it. Auto-slicing from every interface node ran out of memory in the 32-bit build (run_0062);
ATLAS> # PDF p.302 "Mesh Considerations": QT mesh encloses the insulator; tunnelling along y (QTUNN.DIR default 0, Table 3-131).
ATLAS> # It extends one point beyond each oxide face (into IWO and into the gate): flush with the faces, ATLAS 5.28 ignored every
ATLAS> # slice ("Part of Quantum tunnelling mesh lies entirely within the oxide. Must enclose oxide", run_0065).
ATLAS> qtx.mesh loc=0 spac=0.2
ATLAS> qtx.mesh loc=24 spac=0.2
ATLAS> qty.mesh loc=-0.0005 spac=0.0005
ATLAS> qty.mesh loc=0.0175 spac=0.0005
